{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SUPERSEDED BY 0347 (commit 2cc67998e7, landed concurrently). Decisive experiment run on clean origin/main @ b3bbfecbc4, WITHOUT this ticket's change.\n\nExperiment: forced every `git fetch` inside `rebar._snapshot.repo_snapshot` to raise `subprocess.TimeoutExpired`, then let the REAL `materialize_tickets` run as the gate body so the exception reaching the adapter is genuinely produced by the snapshot code under a real forced timeout (not a fabricated one), then drove `voter.review_and_vote` repeatedly against a fake Gerrit.\n\nResult on origin/main:\n  ADAPTER  decision = BLOCK | gap_reason = 'review-error'\n  pass 1: status='deferred'  votes=[]\n  pass 2: status='deferred'  votes=[]\n  pass 3: status='voted'     votes=[-1]   (3-attempt budget exhausted)\n  pass 4: status='skipped'   votes=[-1]\n\nSo a single transient fetch stall NO LONGER casts a durable -1: it defers vote-less, and a vote-less change is exactly what reconcile.py's backfill pre-filter re-drives. The reported defect is fixed on main.\n\nWhy this ticket's mechanism is not additionally needed:\n\n* 0347 keys on the adapter's machine-readable `gap_reason`, and `_block(\"review-error\", ...)` is what the adapter returns for ANY exception out of `produce_code_review_verdict`. `review-error` is in `adapter.RETRYABLE_GAP_REASONS` = {gate-disabled, llm-unavailable, review-error, scanner}.\n* Verified that `gate_source.py:99` lets the fail-closed snapshot error PROPAGATE (\"Fail-closed errors propagate, like the code snapshot\"), so a fetch stall reaches the adapter's except rather than being converted into a terminal `indeterminate`. That was the one residual gap that could have kept this ticket alive; it does not exist.\n* 0347's coverage is a STRICT SUPERSET of this ticket's exception-type classifier. Verified: a deterministic `RuntimeError(\"prompt template missing\")` - which this ticket's `_is_retryable_infra` deliberately classified NON-retryable and would have voted -1 on immediately - also defers on main. There is no fault this ticket's classifier catches that 0347 misses; it can only ever be narrower.\n* 0347's design is also better at this decision point: the deferral is BOUNDED (3 attempts, then an escalated -1 plus a VOTER_ERROR), whereas this ticket's ABSTAIN never escalated and would have left a permanently broken bot silently vote-less forever.\n\nConclusion: duplicate of 0347. Commit 7065736f4b (branch fix/df2c-fetch-timeout, never pushed to Gerrit) is retired unlanded rather than rebased - landing it would put a second, narrower mechanism at the same decision point.\n\nResidual (NOT this bug, and not filed): under 0347 a deterministic review-error burns 3 pointless retry cycles before escalating. That is a latency/efficiency nuance on the failure path, bounded and observable, with no evidence it matters in practice.\n\nChild 12e4-8c74-a738-4014 (abort a stalled git fetch in seconds instead of burning the 300s timeout) is UNAFFECTED and still worth doing: 0347 stops the stall from being durable, but a stalled review still costs 300s and 0347 only tolerates 3 of them."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785712397573978001,"uuid":"7c889b81-1de6-4c2c-8c9e-847191c4720e"}